## Phase 1 — Workspace Architecture & Layout (Foundation)

### Goal: Three-column layout with 3 view modes (Report, Data, Model)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This phase is the structural foundation. Everything else builds on top of it.

#### [MODIFY] [LandingPage.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Downloads/25_osa/one-stop-analytics-saa-s-frontend/frontend/src/pages/LandingPage.jsx)
- Add a **left-side view switcher** with 3 icons: Report View, Data View, Model View
- Switch the main canvas area based on the `activeView` state
- In **Report View**: show current [BIDashboardCanvas](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Downloads/25_osa/one-stop-analytics-saa-s-frontend/frontend/src/components/BIDashboardCanvas.jsx#5-105)
- In **Data View**: show `DataPreviewPanel` (already exists)
- In **Model View**: show new `BIModelView` component (relationship diagram)

#### [NEW] `BIModelView.jsx` + `BIModelView.css`
- Render a visual ERD-style diagram of dataset tables
- Show column names and types for each table
- Allow drag between columns to "create relationships" (visual only, stored as state)
- Display cardinality labels (1:1, 1:M, M:M)

#### [MODIFY] [BIVisualizationsFieldsPanel.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Downloads/25_osa/one-stop-analytics-saa-s-frontend/frontend/src/components/BIVisualizationsFieldsPanel.jsx)
- Split into three sub-panels: **Visualizations**, **Fields**, **Filters**
- Add tab switching between them on the right panel

