## Phase 3 — Report View Enhancements (Canvas Interactions)

### Goal: Full drag-and-drop, multi-page, formatting, interactions

#### [MODIFY] [BIDashboardCanvas.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Downloads/25_osa/one-stop-analytics-saa-s-frontend/frontend/src/components/BIDashboardCanvas.jsx)
- Add **multi-page support**: tab bar at the bottom (Page 1, Page 2 ... + button to add page)
- Allow **resize of visual cards** using resize handles
- Add **drag to reposition** visuals on canvas
- Layer controls: Bring Forward / Send Backward (z-index management)
- Align & Distribute tools (triggered from View ribbon)
- Visual selection: click to select a visual, show selection border + format panel

#### [NEW] `BIFormatPane.jsx` + `BIFormatPane.css`
- Right panel (replaces Fields pane when a visual is selected)
- Visual formatting options: title, background, border, font, legend, data labels, axis formatting, color

#### [NEW] `BIFiltersPane.jsx` + `BIFiltersPane.css`
- Right panel showing 3 filter levels: Visual-level, Page-level, Report-level
- Drag field to add filter, set filter conditions (is, is not, is blank, top N, etc.)

#### [MODIFY] [BIVisualizationsFieldsPanel.jsx](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/Downloads/25_osa/one-stop-analytics-saa-s-frontend/frontend/src/components/BIVisualizationsFieldsPanel.jsx)
- Complete visual type grid: all chart types shown as icons matching Power BI
- Drag field from Fields pane onto a visual → auto-bind the field as X/Y/Value
- Values/Legend/Axis/Tooltip drop zones shown when a visual is selected

